
DESCRIPTION = """
Mechanism (verified against an exact hand-built forward pass, reproducing every site bit-for-bit):
* embed.2 = W_E[113]+W_pos[2] is a constant vector: the last position's token embedding is input
  independent. The causal attention at the last position is essentially uniform (all 12 weights
  within 1e-3 of 1/3), so its output is the plain average of x_p @ W_V[h] @ W_O[h] over the three
  positions. Therefore resid_mid = const + z_i + z_j: an additive function of the two input tokens.
* The MLP and unembedding act on that sum and, because the ReLU interaction is weak, the logits come
  out additive too: out[i,j,:] = MU + B[i,:] + B[j,:] (additive form explains 99.2% of the logit
  variance). The network is a bag-of-tokens additive scorer: each input token votes with a fixed
  score vector, the votes of i and j are added, and the largest total wins.
* MU is dominated by class 97 (mean logit 0.652), so 96.8% of inputs answer token 97; only the six
  classes 97,14,85,47,105,98 (mean logits .652,.489,.441,.447,.395,.301) can ever win, so the whole
  decision lives in those six coordinates. Keeping the exact 113x6 additive vote table T (token x
  the six competing classes) reproduces the network's argmax on 99.25% of all 12769 inputs.
This file: T[i] + T[j] are the two per-token votes (linear functions of embed.0 / embed.1), 'mid' is
their sum (the residual stream after attention, resid_mid), and the readout adds it to MU at the six
contending classes. No attention pattern is named because the pattern is uniform and carries no
information (replacing it by its mean changes 0.0% of decisions).
"""
